                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <p>Letters from Guayaquil received by the Journal Las Noticias confirm the account
                    published by <hi rendition="#italic">la Epoca</hi> up to the 30th December. No
                    demonstration or attempt of any kind had been made against our squadron in the
                    Pacific, and according to the statement of its commandant he had no fears
                    whatever of being attacked. The 16th, three days after the departure of the
                    mail, the vessels destined to increase our force in those seas ought to arrive;
                    and on the other hand, our vice-admiral had received from the commandant of the
                    French fleet offers of service of every sort if he should have need of
                        them.—(<hi rendition="#italic">Idem.</hi>)</p>
            </div>
